{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clearing denominators clearing denominators","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md","fileName":"Clearing Denominators.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clearing Denominators","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Equations and Modeling]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Cross Multiplication","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clearing denominators clearing denominators","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md","fileName":"Clearing Denominators.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clearing Denominators","heading":"Clearing Denominators","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Clearing denominators multiplies every term on both sides of an equation by a common multiple of the denominators. Using the least common multiple usually keeps coefficients smallest.\n\nThe method converts a fractional equation into an equivalent form without fractions. Every term must receive the multiplier, including constants and terms outside visible fractions. Denominators containing variables require restrictions because the multiplier may be zero at excluded values. [[Cross Multiplication]] is a compact special case for an equation consisting of one fraction on each side.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Equations and Modeling","Cross Multiplication","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clearing Denominators.md::2